  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1110</x>
      <y>760</y>
      <w>410</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Adapts a LangChain4j ChatModel (Anthropic for cloud,
Ollama for local) to LlmClient, converting LlmRequest
and LlmResponse to and from the library's message and
tool types. The rest of the system never sees library
types. Clients keep no state between calls, so they
are thread-safe.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1120</x>
      <y>1030</y>
      <w>390</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Returns one cached client per ModelSettings: the
decorated chain for CLOUD, a plain client for LOCAL.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>550</x>
      <y>1040</y>
      <w>390</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>A Message has a role (user, assistant, or tool), its
content, and the source files the content came from,
which RedactingLlmClient uses to withhold local-only
content. A ToolCall names a tool and its arguments.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
